---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { AreaChart } from "astro-ink";

const signups = [
  { label: "Jan", value: 30 },
  { label: "Feb", value: 34 },
  { label: "Mar", value: 42 },
  { label: "Apr", value: 45 },
  { label: "May", value: 52 },
  { label: "Jun", value: 58 },
  { label: "Jul", value: 61 },
  { label: "Aug", value: 70 },
  { label: "Sep", value: 78 },
  { label: "Oct", value: 88 },
  { label: "Nov", value: 102 },
  { label: "Dec", value: 120 },
];

const weekly = [
  { label: "Mon", value: 12 },
  { label: "Tue", value: 18 },
  { label: "Wed", value: 15 },
  { label: "Thu", value: 22 },
  { label: "Fri", value: 30 },
  { label: "Sat", value: 28 },
  { label: "Sun", value: 20 },
];
---
<Base title="AreaChart">
  <div class="docs-page">
    <h1>AreaChart</h1>
    <p class="docs-lede">
      A trend line with the volume underneath filled. Monthly signups below
      are honest sample data, rendered as a static SVG with no tooltips.
    </p>

    <h2>Monthly signups</h2>
    <div class="docs-example">
      <AreaChart data={signups} />
    </div>
    <pre class="docs-code"><code>&lt;AreaChart data=&#123;signups&#125; /&gt;</code></pre>

    <h2>With values</h2>
    <p>Pass <code>showValues</code> to print each value above its point.</p>
    <div class="docs-example">
      <AreaChart label="Weekly signups" data={weekly} showValues />
    </div>
    <pre class="docs-code"><code>&lt;AreaChart label="Weekly signups" data=&#123;weekly&#125; showValues /&gt;</code></pre>

    <h2>Props</h2>
    <table class="docs-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>data</code></td><td><code>Array&lt;&#123; label: string; value: number &#125;&gt;</code></td><td>-</td><td>Points in order, left to right.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>width</code></td><td><code>number</code></td><td><code>560</code></td><td>viewBox width; the SVG scales to <code>100%</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>height</code></td><td><code>number</code></td><td><code>240</code></td><td>viewBox height.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>label</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td><code>"Area chart"</code></td><td>Chart name; opens the auto-summary.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>showValues</code></td><td><code>boolean</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Print each value above its point.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>class</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>-</td><td>Style passthrough.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Static honesty</h2>
    <p>
      Static SVG, no tooltips; values appear in text only when
      <code>showValues</code> is set. The fill is the accent at 25% via
      <code>color-mix</code>, closed to the zero baseline. X labels longer
      than 8 characters are truncated with the full text kept in a
      <code>&lt;title&gt;</code>. The baseline is clamped into the viewBox,
      so negative values (not shown in the demos) fill below it.
    </p>

    <h2>Accessibility</h2>
    <ul class="docs-list">
      <li>The chart is an image (<code>role="img"</code>) with an auto-summary label: <code>"&#123;Label&#125;, &#123;n&#125; points, high &#123;maxLabel&#125; &#123;max&#125;, low &#123;minLabel&#125; &#123;min&#125;"</code>.</li>
      <li>A <code>&lt;title&gt;</code> repeats the summary and a <code>&lt;desc&gt;</code> describes the reading order.</li>
      <li>Every point carries a <code>&lt;title&gt;</code> with its <code>"&#123;label&#125;: &#123;value&#125;"</code>.</li>
      <li>Y ticks come from <code>niceTicks</code>; tick and axis text uses the muted token at xs size.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</Base>
